# ---- Numbers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spoken number words, nominative masculine (the neuter "jedno" and the feminine "jedna", "dwie" are
# forms below). 21-99 compose as "{tens} {units}" ("dwadzieścia trzy"), 101-999 as "{hundreds} {rest}"
# ("sto dwadzieścia"); every hundred is listed. Compound numbers ending in 1 keep "jeden" in every
# gender and case ("dwadzieścia jeden partii", "z dwudziestoma jeden błędami").
# Forms ("{n:form}" looks up number.<n>.<form>.spoken first, else the plain word): the counted nouns
# below use them, and a line can use the bare ones (count.<form> routes each plural slot right):
#   f         jedna, dwie (22 = dwadzieścia dwie)        "{n:f}" = feminine nominative
#   neut      jedno                                      "{n:neut}" = neuter nominative
#   acc_f     jedną, dwie                                "{n:acc_f}" = feminine accusative
#   acc_anim  jednego, dwa                               "{n:acc_anim}" = accusative of an animate noun
#   gen       jednego, dwóch, pięciu, dwudziestu jeden   "{n:gen}" (gen_f: jednej)
#   dat       jednemu, dwóm, pięciu                      "{n:dat}" (dat_f: jednej)
#   ins       jednym, dwoma, pięcioma                    "{n:ins}" (ins_f: jedną, dwiema)
#   loc       jednym, dwóch, pięciu                      "{n:loc}" (loc_f: jednej): "mat w {n:loc}"
#   ord       pierwszy, dwudziesty pierwszy              "{n:ord}" (and ord_gen, ord_loc), see below
# The case forms are exact for 0-100 and the round hundreds; 101-999 compose with the hundreds word in
# the nominative ("sto dwóch" for "stu dwóch"): no count in these cases reaches them.
