# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Polish plural rule (assets/i18n): one (only 1) | few (2-4, 22-24, 32-34 ... but not 12-14) | many
# (0, 5-21, 25-31 ...). After 5+ (and 0) the nominative and accusative take the genitive plural
# ("pięć ruchów"); compound numbers ending in 1 are "many" ("dwadzieścia jeden ruchów").
# Every counted noun has six cases: count.<noun> (nominative), and count.<noun>_acc, _gen, _dat, _ins,
# _loc: "{n:move}" = "trzy ruchy", "mat w {m:move_loc}" = "mat w trzech ruchach", "{n:piece_acc}" =
# "jedną bierkę / dwie bierki / pięć bierek", "z {n:mistake_ins}" = "z dwoma błędami".
# Nouns: ruch, punkt (m); pionek, szach (m, animate accusative "jednego pionka", "dać szacha"); bierka
# (f: any chessman, pawns included), niedokładność, partia, pozycja (f); pole, bicie (n); raz (m);
# "gruby błąd" (blunder), "najlepszy ruch" (a run of best moves), "atakująca bierka" (attacker) and
# "broniąca bierka" (defender; "obrońca" is the word for one defending piece, but counted it would
# need the personal forms "dwóch obrońców").
